  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/32-all-the-rest/monodactylus-kottelati-2/",
      "html": "<p>Monos are classics among the brackish water fishes. Kept in brackish water at about 26-28°C, these racehorses among the fishes will bring only joy for the keeper. It reaches a length of up to 20 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/32-all-the-rest/monodactylus-kottelati-2/",
      "html": "<p>Monodactylus kottelati is currently imported quite often from Thailand.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/32-all-the-rest/monodactylus-kottelati-2/",
      "html": "<p>It should be kept in a large tank.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/32-all-the-rest/monodactylus-kottelati-2/",
      "html": "<p>Much of the aquarium literature mentions that these fish can be adapted easily to freshwater. But what should this be good for? It is not difficult to put some salt (10-20 g per litre) in the water. Keep them in brackish water at a water temperature of about 26-28°C.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/32-all-the-rest/monodactylus-kottelati-2/",
      "html": "<p>This fish should be kept in a large school of conspecifics. Otherwise they can be very quarrelsome.</p>"
    }
  ],
